      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Prader-Willi syndrome, due to microdeletion of proximal 15q, is a well-known cause of syndromic obesity."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE CHARACTERISTICS",
          "content": "A couple with history of repeated first trimester abortions had a son with balanced Robertsonian translocation of chromosomes 13 and 15 according to cytogenetic banding technique."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Chromosomal analysis for the couple was performed. A balanced translocation involving BP1-BP3 region of proximal 15q was observed in the father."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "Investigations of the parents is mandatory when a structural rearrangement is detected in a dysmorphic child."
        }
      ]},
